10}], "blurhash": "UlLOD;Dix[tl?wpIjaoJ-.j]aiV]ofs+j]V?", "full_resolution": [635, 800]}, "title": "Flower's Ms Hostin", "last_comment_created": 1790438957467, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": true, "comments": 1, "score_up": 97, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATVQvn1wQ", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 14, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8857402, "raw_content": "So there's a lot of people disappointed at the state of politics currently with the Republicans, but people may feel like there's nothing they can do about the situation or that all they can do is \"wait\" for things to improve\n\nThere's definitely a lot we can do to speed things up though, with varying degrees of success\n\nThere are political solutions (run for office, run campaigns, lobby your politicians, etc.)\n\nand non-political solutions (\"vote with your wallet\", build up your community, expose fraud like Nick Shirley, etc.)\n\nSo let's talk about what we can actually do to speed things up and to personally take action to improve our country, if you'd like, rather than feel helpless and powerless and like we can do nothing \n\nAll we can do is the little we can do, but if everyone does a little bit, that can add up to having a big impact\n\nedit: we don't need to \"wait\" in general - while one thing is \"cooking\", we can go work on another. Or take a break and live life (rest can be essential as well). But let's keep up the high energy and MAGA momentum even if our elected reps may not reflect the energy our base has like on this site and elsewhere!", "author": "bluewhiteandred", "created": 1790455648347, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Radical_covfefe", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Discuss: Things We Can Do to Speed Up Resolutions to Political Issues", "last_comment_created": 1790460026103, "content": "<p>So there's a lot of people disappointed at the state of politics currently with the Republicans, but people may feel like there's nothing they can do about the situation or that all they can do is &quot;wait&quot; for things to improve</p>\n<p>There's definitely a lot we can do to speed things up though, with varying degrees of success</p>\n<p>There are political solutions (run for office, run campaigns, lobby your politicians, etc.)</p>\n<p>and non-political solutions (&quot;vote with your wallet&quot;, build up your community, expose fraud like Nick Shirley, etc.)</p>\n<p>So let's talk about what we can actually do to speed things up and to personally take action to improve our country, if you'd like, rather than feel helpless and powerless and like we can do nothing</p>\n<p>All we can do is the little we can do, but if everyone does a little bit, that can add up to having a big impact</p>\n<p>edit: we don't need to &quot;wait&quot; in general - while one thing is &quot;cooking&quot;, we can go work on another. Or take a break and live life (rest can be essential as well). But let's keep up the high energy and MAGA momentum even if our elected reps may not reflect the energy our base has like on this site and elsewhere!</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 9, "score_up": 14, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"sta